982_campus-life_lw.rev.1768774382.jpg 3x\" data-max-w=\"1920\" data-max-h=\"1080\" loading=\"lazy\" data-optimized=\"true\"\/>\n<\/picture>\n","image_info":["181","16982_campus-life_lw","jpg","1","0,0,1920,1080","","","1","Campus Life"]},{"id":"380642","ts_start":1775142000,"ts_end":1775178000,"tz":"America\/Chicago","tz_abbrv":"CDT","tz_offset":-18000,"tz2_offset":-18000,"tz_format":"us","href":"event\/380642-outdoor-pool","title":"Outdoor Pool","status":"1","location":"","summary":"","is_starred":"","image_src":"","image_raw":""},{"id":"380604","ts_start":1775145600,"ts_end":1775149200,"tz":"America\/Chicago","tz_abbrv":"CDT","tz_offset":-18000,"tz2_offset":-18000,"tz_format":"us","href":"event\/380604-ece-faculty-candidate-seminar-decoding-quantum","title":"ECE Faculty Candidate Seminar - \u201cDecoding Quantum Error-Correcting Codes\u201d","status":"1","location":"Wisenbaker Engineering Building","has_map":1,"latitude":"30.620771","longitude":"-96.338948","summary":"<p data-path-to-node=\"0\">\n  Discover the future of scalable quantum computing in this ECE Faculty Candidate Seminar featuring Dr. Hanwen Yao from Duke University. As quantum computing nears a transformative era, the challenge of protecting fragile data from noise remains a primary hurdle; this session dives into Quantum Low-Density Parity-Check (QLDPC) codes as a high-efficiency alternative to traditional methods. Dr. Yao will introduce his innovative BP-Guided Decimation (BPGD) algorithm, demonstrating how it turns the complex issue of quantum degeneracy into a decoding advantage. Whether you are an expert in coding theory or new to the field, this talk offers a comprehensive look at the algorithms paving the way toward practical, fault-tolerant quantum systems.\n<\/p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"1\">\n  <li>\n    <p data-path-to-node=\"1,0,0\">\n      <strong data-path-to-node=\"1,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Date:<\/strong> Thursday, April 2, 2026\n    <\/p>\n  <\/li>\n  <li>\n    <p data-path-t