-sheets-root=\"1\">Ginessa Payne, Center for Teaching Excellence<br \/>\n  <br \/>\n  <strong>Description:<\/strong> Eighth in a series of workshops for graduate students, post-docs, and visiting scholars whose primary language is not English. This interactive workshop teaches the value of a well-managed class discussion and provides functional language for leading such a discussion.<br \/>\n  <br \/>\n  It also introduces a critical aspect of pronunciation, which is the linking of one word to the next.<br \/>\n  <br \/>\n  <strong>Learning Outcomes:<\/strong> Participants will be able to\u2026<br \/>\n  <br \/>\n  1. In a class discussion, react and respond appropriately to keep the discussion advancing.<br \/>\n  <br \/>\n  2. Pronounce phrases with connected speech (linking consonant to consonant, linking consonant to vowel, and linking vowel to vowel across word boundaries).<br \/>\n  <br \/>\n  <strong>Register Here:<\/strong> <a class=\"in-cell-link\" href=\"https:\/\/ers.tamu.edu\/event\/11783\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https:\/\/ers.tamu.edu\/event\/1178<\/a><a class=\"in-cell-link\" href=\"https:\/\/ers.tamu.edu\/event\/11783\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">3<\/a>&#160;<\/span>\n<\/p>","is_starred":"","image_src":"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/gid\/38\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,1280,720\/16731_LiveWhale_Picture.rev.1765295412.png","image_raw":"<picture class=\"lw_image\">\n\t<source type=\"image\/webp\" srcset=\"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/2x\/gid\/38\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,1280,720\/16731_LiveWhale_Picture.rev.1765295412.webp 2x, https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/3x\/gid\/38\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/1\/src_region\/0,0,1280,720\/16731_LiveWhale_Picture.rev.1765295412.webp 3x\" data-origin=\"responsive\"\/>\n\t<source type=\"image\/png\" srcset=\"https:\/\/calendar.tamu.edu\/live\/image\/scale\/2x\/gid\/38\/width\/200\/height\/200\/crop\/